{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Cursed are you from the ground.</b> Cursed and deprived of the ground's goodness." "<b>Which opened its mouth.</b> Which you used to cover your brother's killing — and accordingly you shall no longer use it as you did before for your life's needs. There was no need to specify the murderer's punishment, for the law is self-evident in nature regarding every wrongdoer: כַּאֲשֶׁר עָשָׂה כֵּן יֵעָשֶׂה לוֹ (Leviticus 24:19)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:07.257064252Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}